          Hail!<br>
          The Knights of Eternal Vigilance located on the Luclin server are planning a raid on Crushbone for Saturday, April 15th at 11am PST.  Located in the scenic lands of Gfay is a cozy getaway known as Clan Crushbone.  This remarkably quaint outdoor dungeon features a Castle with an exterior moat for swimming practice, a Slaver house for anyone into whips and chains, and a hill where you may receive educational training in the fighting arts (Trainer Hill).  Unfortunately, a lot of rather unruly orcs have infested this resort getaway and will need to be cleared out before we begin the sunbathing and volleyball tournaments.  We will all meet at the orc lift in the Elven city of Kelethin before making our way into Crushbone proper.  Afterwards, there will be the traditional lotto (2pp each entry fee with half the prize money going to the winner), along with a scavenger hunt and a drunken race through the treetop city (SoW’s and Levitate provided free of course).  The rules for the scavenger hunt and the race will be released prior to each event.<br>
          <br>
            Everyone is encouraged to come out to our first event and meet the people behind the guild.  Free drinks and food will be passed around and we will be encouraging new members to apply as well.  Also, please RSVP so that we have enough alcohol/food on-hand as well as to provide you with transportation if you have need.  If you have any questions concerning the guild or the event come to our web site at The Knights of Eternal Vigilance or email me directly at Circadian@Luclin.com.  Hope to see you there! <br>
